AHS-003 — Architectural Views

Document ID: AHS-003
Title: Architectural Views
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical architectural views used to describe, analyze, communicate, and implement the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

Architectural views provide complementary perspectives of the Atlas architecture, enabling stakeholders to understand the system according to their responsibilities without altering the underlying architecture.

Each view addresses a distinct set of concerns while remaining consistent with the canonical concepts defined by ACC and the architectural principles defined by AHS.

2. Scope

This specification applies to all Atlas architectural documentation.

Every architectural description SHALL be expressed through one or more of the canonical architectural views defined herein.

3. Architectural View Model

The Atlas architecture SHALL be described using the following six canonical views:

                    Atlas Architecture
                           │
 ┌───────────────┬──────────┼──────────┬──────────────┐
 │               │          │          │              │
 ▼               ▼          ▼          ▼              ▼
Conceptual    Logical    Information  Process    Deployment
 View          View         View        View         View
                           │
                           ▼
                    Implementation
                         View

Each view answers a different architectural question.

