10. Relationship Between Views

The architectural views are complementary.

No individual view completely describes the Atlas architecture.

Together they provide a complete architectural description.

Conceptual View
        │
        ▼
Logical View
        │
        ▼
Information View
        │
        ▼
Process View
        │
        ▼
Deployment View
        │
        ▼
Implementation View

Each successive view refines the previous one without changing its semantics.

11. View Consistency

All architectural views SHALL:

Conform to ACC.
Conform to AHS principles.
Preserve conceptual integrity.
Avoid contradictory representations.
Maintain traceability across views.

A change in one view that affects another SHALL be reflected consistently.

12. Conformance

An architectural description conforms to this specification if it:

Uses one or more canonical architectural views.
Preserves consistency across views.
Maintains semantic alignment with ACC.
Documents assumptions and constraints.
13. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce additional specialized views (for example, security, performance, or operational views), provided they complement rather than replace the canonical views.